The false-postcondition mutation compiled cleanly, then failed with exit 1 at the intended result mismatch: execution reached `"YES"` while the mutated claim required `"NO"` under a satisfiable `1 >= 1` guard. The proof is therefore discriminating. I’m assembling the final seven-stage review and trust ledger now; no soundness or domain-narrowing defect has emerged.
